-- title:
--   Conjugates of m-th roots of unity are Frobenius powers
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and an intermediate field $K$ of the extension $\mathbb{Q}_q \subseteq$ `PadicAlgCl q` (an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}_q$) which is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}_q$. Write $R_w =$ `Rw q K` for the valuation subring of $K$ obtained by pulling back, along the structure map $K \to$ `PadicAlgCl q`, the valuation subring of the canonical valuation on `PadicAlgCl q` with values in $\mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}$; thus $R_w$ is the ring of elements of $K$ of valuation at most $1$, and `IsLocalRing.ResidueField (Rw q K)` is its residue field. Let $m$ be a natural number not divisible by $q$ (so in particular $m \neq 0$), let $\zeta_0 \in$ `PadicAlgCl q` be a primitive $m$-th root of unity, and let $t \in$ `PadicAlgCl q` lie in the root set over `PadicAlgCl q` of the minimal polynomial of $\zeta_0$ over $K$. The conclusion is that there exists a natural number $i$ with $t = \zeta_0^{Q^i}$, where $Q =$ `Nat.card (IsLocalRing.ResidueField (Rw q K))` is the cardinality of the residue field of $R_w$.
--
--   This is the statement that the Galois action on the $m$-th roots of unity, $m$ prime to $q$, in a finite extension $K$ of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ proceeds through powers of the Frobenius $\zeta \mapsto \zeta^{Q}$ of the residue field, i.e. that $K(\mu_m)/K$ is unramified with Galois group generated by Frobenius. It is used to compute the degree $[K(\mu_m):K]$ as the multiplicative order of $Q$ modulo $m$, in [`IntermediateField.finrank_adjoin_rootsOfUnity_padic_eq_orderOf`](thm.html#IntermediateField.finrank_adjoin_rootsOfUnity_padic_eq_orderOf).
